<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section xml:id="sp-combined-events">
  <title>Combined Events (HL)</title>

  <objectives>
    <title>Learning Outcomes</title>
    <ul>
      <li><xref ref="lo-sp-7" /> — Sample spaces for two events (HL)</li>
      <li><xref ref="lo-sp-8" /> — Combined events (HL)</li>
    </ul>
  </objectives>

  <p>
    For two independent events, construct a <term>sample space</term> — a systematic list or table of all possible outcomes.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Example:</strong> Rolling two dice. The sample space has <m>6 \times 6 = 36</m> equally likely outcomes.
  </p>
  <p>
    For independent events <m>A</m> and <m>B</m>:
    <me>P(A \text{ and } B) = P(A) \times P(B)</me>
  </p>
  <p>
    For mutually exclusive events (cannot both happen):
    <me>P(A \text{ or } B) = P(A) + P(B)</me>
  </p>

  <exercises xml:id="exs-combined-events">
    <title>Exercises</title>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-two-dice">
      <statement><p>Two fair dice are rolled. Find the probability that the sum equals 7.</p></statement>
      <answer><p><m>\frac{1}{6}</m></p></answer>
      <solution><p>Outcomes giving sum 7: (1,6),(2,5),(3,4),(4,3),(5,2),(6,1) — that's 6 outcomes out of 36. <m>P = \frac{6}{36} = \frac{1}{6}</m>.</p></solution>
    </exercise>

    <exercise xml:id="ex-coin-die">
      <statement><p>A coin is flipped and a die is rolled. Find the probability of getting heads and a 6.</p></statement>
      <answer><p><m>\frac{1}{12}</m></p></answer>
      <solution><p><m>P(\text{heads}) \times P(6) = \frac{1}{2} \times \frac{1}{6} = \frac{1}{12}</m>.</p></solution>
    </exercise>

  </exercises>

</section>
